<title>HONG KONG: China Inv issues shares to buy property.</title>
<headline>China Inv issues shares to buy property.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property concern China Investments Holdings Ltd said it had agreed to buy a commercial building on Hong Kong Queen's Road West from third party Sherson Development Ltd for HK$99.60 million.</p>
<p>HK$44.6 million will be paid by an issue of 54.39 million new shares at HK$0.82 per share, and the balance is to be paid in cash, China Investment said.</p>
<p>On completion of the deal, Sherson will hold 54.39 million shares or 12.25 percent of the enlarged share capital of China Investment, it said.</p>
<p>The property is a 19-storey commercial building erected over a 4-storey commercial office podium in Queen's Road West.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
